menu "Linux Bridge Exporter (Power Base -> Linux OTBR host)"

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Bounded TOPOLOGY export event queue depth"
        default 32
        help
            Depth of the FIFO queue between power_base_transport's
            on_topology_applied/on_node_offline bridge-observer callbacks
            (OT-task context, non-blocking enqueue only) and this
            component's own sending task. A full queue drops the newest
            TOPOLOGY event with a rate-limited warning rather than blocking
            the OT task or halting anything -- see
            components/linux_bridge_exporter's own header comment. The
            periodic full topology resync below recovers any dropped event.
            (Correction pass: SAMPLE events no longer share this queue at
            all -- see PENDING_SAMPLES_MAX in linux_bridge_exporter.c, a
            fixed-size, always-coalescing-by-uuid table sized to
            SENSOR_ROOT_AGGREGATOR_MAX_NODES, not a Kconfig value.)

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_FULL_RESYNC_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Full topology + latest-sample resync interval (ms)"
        default 5000
        help
            Every this many ms, resend every topology_registry node's
            CURRENT state AND every sensor_root_aggregator node's CURRENT
            (most recent) sample to the Linux host, regardless of whether
            anything changed -- recovers from a dropped/coalesced-away
            event, a stale/rebuilt Linux registry, or a Linux OTBR host that
            just restarted, without waiting for that module's next sensor
            measurement (this follow-up's own explicit requirement).

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Bridge exporter heartbeat interval (ms)"
        default 10000
        help
            Liveness-only signal (power_base_uuid + uptime_ms + node_count);
            never authoritative -- the periodic full resync above is what
            actually reconciles Linux-side state.

    config LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_SAMPLE_MIN_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Minimum interval between two SAMPLE exports for the SAME module_uuid (ms)"
        default 1000
        help
            Transport-load reduction (Power Base -> Linux, this pass): caps
            how often this component actually SENDS a SAMPLE export for any
            one module_uuid, regardless of how often that module's sensor
            measurement/aggregator storage updates -- neither the sensor
            measurement period nor the aggregator's own storage rate is
            changed by this setting, only how often the ALREADY-STORED
            latest value is mirrored to the Linux host. Rapid samples for
            the same uuid within this window keep coalescing (upsert,
            latest-wins, see PENDING_SAMPLES_MAX) exactly as before; once
            the window reopens, the then-current latest value is sent --
            never a replayed backlog of older values. TOPOLOGY events
            (ATTACHED/UPDATED/DETACHED/OFFLINE, parent-state changes) are
            NOT subject to this limit -- they are always sent immediately,
            see s_topology_pending_*/s_topology_queue. The periodic full
            resync (LINUX_BRIDGE_EXPORTER_FULL_RESYNC_INTERVAL_MS, far
            longer than this by default) is independent of this per-uuid
            gate and always sends every node's current value.

endmenu
